Since $A$ is a singleton, the fault domain $\U^A$ is empty.
The fault domain $\U^A_0$ only contains Mealy machines with a single state, and self-loop transitions for inputs $a$ and $b$.  Test suite $T$ verifies that the outputs of these transitions are in agreement with $\Spec$.  Thus, any machine in $\U^A_0$ that passes $T$ will be equivalent to $\Spec$. Hence $T$ is $0$-$A$-complete.
