The next lemma, a variation of the classical result of \cite{Pa81}, is easy to prove.
\begin{lemma}
	\label{la:bisimulation}
	Let $\M, \N$ be Mealy machines.
	Then $\M \simeq \N$ iff $\M \approx \N$.
\end{lemma}

The next lemmas give some useful properties of a basis.

\begin{lemma}
	\label{f restricted to B injective}
	Suppose $\Obs$ is an observation tree for $\M$ with $f \colon \Obs \to \M$ and basis $B$. Then $f$ restricted to $B$ is injective.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
	Let $q$ and $q'$ be two distinct states in $B$.  Since $q \apart q'$, we may conclude by Lemma~\ref{la: apartness refinement} that $f(q) \apart  f(q')$. Thus in particular $f(q) \neq f(q')$ and so $f$ restricted to $B$ is injective.
\end{proof}



