		By the definition of a separating family, $W_s \cap W_t$ contains a separating sequence $\rho$ for $s$ and $t$.
		Since $A \cdot  I^{\leq k+1} \odot {\cal W} \subseteq T$, $\delta^{\Obs}(q, \rho) \downarrow$ and $\delta^{\Obs}(r, \rho) \downarrow$.
