\section{{Concluding remarks}}
{In this work we have addressed the construction and analysis of virtual element schemes for viscoelasticity with weakly imposed stress. We have shown the well-posedness of the problem and have established stability and convergence of the proposed discretisation. Some numerical tests were showcased to confirm the properties of the schemes. Future work includes the coupling with reaction-diffusion mechanisms in view of applications into mechano-chemical calcium dynamics in epithelial cell compounds, the analysis for arbitrarily small edges following \cite{brenner18}, the extension to stabilisation-free formulations, and also the design of strongly symmetric stress virtual element spaces following the appealing hybrid approaches from, e.g., \cite{visinoni24}.}



