\section{Proposed Method}
\subsection{Region-Adaptive Latent Upsampling}
\label{subsec:RALU}
% To mitigate the high computational cost associated with the early stages of denoising in diffusion models, we initiate the generative process from low-resolution latents, specifically downsampled by a factor of 2 in each spatial dimension relative to the original resolution. This design choice enables rapid initial sampling while retaining the global structure necessary for coherent generation.

As illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:overall_framework}, our approach comprises three progressive stages of region-adaptive latent upsampling, each balancing computational efficiency and generative fidelity.

% \textbf{Stage 1: Coarse-level sampling to accelerate.}
