To verify if a solution $\mu^{(i+1)} := \mu^{(i,l^{(i)})}$, with $l^{(i)}$ being the amount of iterates the gradient descent algorithm required to solve the subproblem,  yields a sufficient decrease of the kernel surrogate model $\hat{J}^{(i)}$, we make use of the \ac{agc} point $\mu_{\textnormal{AGC}}^{(i)}$.
