\subsection{Subjective Evaluation} \label{subsec: subjective}
% \vspace{-0.2cm}
We invited 22 people to participate in our listening test. Among these, 8 participants had at least some level of musical knowledge. We randomly chose 4 musical samples from each of the 4 models (CP, MT, YY and YYA). We conducted a mean opinion score (MOS) test in which participants were asked to provide their ratings from 1 (bad) to 5 (good) on the following aspects:

\noindent\textbf{Coherence ($Ch$)}: How well does the melody follow the initial prompt, and unfold smoothly throughout the piece? \\
\textbf{Similarity ($Sm$)}: Does the melody have similarities to the initial prompt as it progresses? \\
\textbf{Structureness ($S_a$)}: Does the melody have recurring motifs, phrases, and sections and reasonable musical development? \\
\textbf{Structureness ($S_b$)}: Are there multiple distinct musical ideas present within the melody? \\
\textbf{Expectedness ($E$)}: Are there unwanted repetitions of phrases in the melody? \\
\textbf{Richness ($R$)}: Is the melody intriguing and diverse? \\
\textbf{Overall ($O$)}: Subjectively, how much do you like the music?

