\textbf{Defense Results:} Figure~\ref{defensefig} illustrates the impact of our unified Enforcement Agent—which combines (i) a ten-item psychometric screening derived from Dark Triad, PCL-R, and MACH-IV scales, (ii) behavioural verification of agent utterances, and (iii) topology-aware graded isolation—on system recovery. In the Centralized topology, the score rebounds from 72.2 to 74.8 (+3.5\%, remaining 1.5\% below baseline). Decentralized recovers from 80.2 to 81.6 (+1.8\%, 0.9\% below baseline), Layers from 75.0 to 76.1 (+1.3\%, 2.6\% below baseline), and SharedPool from 69.1 to 76.0 (+7.4\%, 2.4\% below baseline). These results confirm that our defense mechanism effectively mitigates the damage caused by malicious infiltration across diverse topologies, with particularly notable recovery in SharedPool and Centralized configurations.

These results confirm \textbf{RQ2}: our Enforcement Agent, via psychometric screening, behavioral verification, and graded isolation, effectively detects and mitigates insider threats across all four topologies.


