  The set $\mathcal{S'} =\set{\set{x_1,x_2,x_4}, \set{x_3, x_5, x_6}}$ is an exact $3$-cover of $X$. The thick red edges in the graph show the corresponding matching cut of size~$6q=12$. $X^1$ and $X^2$ are the partition classes of a complete bipartite graph. For readability the edges between $X^1$ and $X^2$ are not represented. }\label{f-np-mmc-biprad}
 \end{center}
