\section{Proposed Approach} \label{prop_approach}
In this section, we describe the proposed methodology for modeling Task-A and Task-B. Task-A is approached as a binary classification problem, where the goal is to determine whether a given input text is human-written or machine-generated. Task-B, on the other hand, aims to identify which LLM generated the input text and is treated as a multi-class classification problem. For Task-A, we fine-tuned OpenAI's GPT\_4o-mini and Google's BERT, whereas for Task-B, we fine-tuned BERT and META's LLAMA-3 8B. The fine-tuning approaches based on simple prompts are explained in the following subsections.

