\subsection{Two-phase methods for QRE programming} \label{subsec:2p}
We proposed two-phase methods for QRE programming in Section \ref{sec:2phase}. For numerical experiments, we have synthesized some problems by fixing $r$ and $n$, and choosing a $n$-by-$r$ matrix $V$ which is all zero except the main diagonal is all ones. Let $E_i \in \S^r$ be a matrix of all zeros except a 1 on the $i$th diagonal entry. Consider problem \eqref{eq:QRE-28} where $M:=I$ and the linear constraints are $x_i \leq 1$ for $i\in \{1,\ldots,k\}$. We define
\[
A_i := VE_iV^\top,  \ \ i \in \{1,\ldots,k\}. 
\]
