\subsection{Human Evaluation of Counselor AIs}

The analysis of human expert evaluations of counselor AIs yielded the following results.

For fixed effects, GPT-zero scored significantly lower than Opus-SMDP across all measures: CCT, PAR, EMP, and OVR showed differences of -0.90 to -1.04 points, while SST showed a smaller difference of -0.50 points (Tables 3 and 4). Compared to GPT-SMDP, GPT-zero demonstrated significantly lower scores on all indices, with CCT/PAR/EMP/OVR showing differences of -0.84 to -1.23 points, while SST showed a smaller difference of -0.34 points. No significant differences were observed between the Opus-SMDP and GPT-SMDP groups. Additionally, neither the client AI age nor gender settings showed significant effects on any measure.
Regarding random effects, inter-rater SD (0.47-0.68 points) was consistently smaller than residual SD (0.81-0.88 points) across all indices (Table 5).

