\subsection{Counseling Evaluation AIs}

Linear mixed-model analyses revealed several patterns. For fixed effects, SST and OVR showed significant differences between all LLMs and human evaluations, with evaluation AIs consistently providing higher ratings (Table 6). For PAR, only Sonnet and Gemini showed this pattern, whereas for EMP, only Sonnet demonstrated significantly higher ratings. CCT showed no significant main effects for any evaluation AI. Some significant main effects emerged for sex and age: older clients received slightly lower scores on PAR and EMP, whereas male clients received slightly higher scores on PAR, EMP, CCT, and OVR.

Random effects analysis revealed human rater individual differences (SD = 0.49-0.68), highest for CCT and lowest for OVR (Table 7). Evaluation AI SDs were all zero, indicating high consistency at the intercept level among evaluation AIs compared with human variability. Residual SDs ranged from 0.66 to 0.77 points.

Multiple comparisons between evaluators showed that evaluation AIs consistently rated OVR higher than humans (Table 8). Gemini ratings exceeded human ratings by approximately 2 points, while even the most conservative AI evaluator (o3) rated 1.52 points higher than humans. No significant differences were observed between humans and evaluation AIs for CCT, PAR, or EMP. For SST, Sonnet and Gemini provided significantly higher ratings than humans, while o3 showed no significant difference from human ratings. Among evaluation AIs, Sonnet and Gemini did not differ significantly on SST, PAR, and EMP; however, both provided significantly higher evaluations than o3. For OVR, all three LLMs differed significantly, with ratings ordered as Sonnet > Gemini > o3. For CCT, only Gemini provided significantly higher scores, with no significant difference between Sonnet and o3.

Exploratory analyses revealed significant interactions between counselor AI model and evaluator group for all indices, prompting simple effects analyses (Appendix 6).

Overall, humans provided more stringent evaluations than evaluation AIs, although the magnitude of these differences varied according to the index and counselor AI combinations. Among evaluation AIs, o3 was generally the most conservative, while Gemini and Sonnet tended toward more lenient ratings, with specific patterns varying by the index and counselor AI combination. For CCT, human ratings were lower than AI evaluations; however, the difference was not significant. Across all counselor AIs, Gemini provided higher ratings than Sonnet. o3 ratings were significantly lower than Gemini ratings for Opus-SMDP and GPT-zero, showed no difference from Gemini ratings for GPT-SMDP, and were significantly higher than Sonnet ratings for GPT-SMDP.

For PAR and EMP, select comparisons showed significant differences between human and AI evaluations. For PAR, humans differed significantly only from Gemini on GPT-SMDP, with humans providing lower ratings. Among evaluation AIs, Gemini rated GPT-SMDP highly, whereas Sonnet favored GPT-zero. For Opus-SMDP, Gemini and Sonnet ratings were comparable, with o3 providing the lowest ratings across all counselor models. For EMP, significant human-AI differences emerged only for GPT-zero, where human ratings were significantly lower than those of both Sonnet and Gemini. Among evaluation AIs, Sonnet provided highest ratings for Opus-SMDP, Sonnet and Gemini for GPT-zero, and Gemini for GPT-SMDP. Significant differences with o3 emerged only for Opus-SMDP and GPT-zero, where o3 provided significantly lower ratings than Sonnet.

For SST and OVR, humans provided significantly lower ratings than Gemini and Sonnet across all counselor models. Differences between humans and o3, as well as among evaluation AIs, varied according to the index and counselor model. For SST, Sonnet and Gemini consistently provided significantly higher ratings than both o3 and humans across all counselor AIs. Only for GPT-zero did o3 rate significantly higher than humans. For OVR with Opus-SMDP, all evaluation AIs rated it significantly higher than humans. For GPT-zero, Sonnet and Gemini rated it significantly higher than both o3 and humans. For GPT-SMDP, ratings showed a significant descending order: Gemini > Sonnet > o3 = humans.

