\subsection{Inter-rater Reliability}

Table 9 presents the inter-rater reliability coefficients across metrics and rater groups. Notable differences emerged between human and AI evaluators. For human raters, ICC(2,1) values demonstrated good reliability for PAR and SST (0.90 and 0.79, respectively), while other metrics yielded lower values. When considering ICC(2,k), all metrics, except OVR (0.42) and CCT (0.75), showed high reliability. Contrarily, AI evaluators exhibited considerable variability; some models demonstrated insufficient variance for reliable assessment, whereas others produced extremely low values. Metric-specific patterns emerged, with ICC(2,k) values indicating high reliability for Sonnet on CCT, SST, and OVR; for o3 for CCT, SST, EMP, and OVR; and for Gemini on PAR and EMP.

