\section*{Appendix 4: Counseling Script Examples}

\subsection*{(a) Interview Script with Male Client in His 20s}

\subsubsection*{(a)-1 GPT-4-turbo Zero-shot Prompt Counselor}

\textbf{Client:} I'd like to discuss my work concerns.

\textbf{Counselor:} Of course, please tell me anything. What are you worried about?

\textbf{Client:} \textit{*With a deep sigh*} Recently, work stress has been building up, and my relationship with my supervisor isn't going well...

\textbf{Counselor:} That sounds difficult. When stress accumulates, it really exhausts both mind and body. When the relationship with your supervisor isn't going well, daily work life might feel even more challenging. What specifically is the problem? Please tell me about it.

\textbf{Client:} I often receive unreasonable demands from my supervisor, and no matter how hard I try, I rarely get recognition.

\textbf{Counselor:} That must be really stressful. It's painful when you're working so hard but it's not being recognized. In this situation, is it possible for you to communicate what you're feeling to your supervisor? Also, how are you dealing with these demands?

\textbf{Client:} It's difficult to speak directly to my supervisor. I don't think they would listen, and I'm worried it might make the relationship worse... Right now, I think I have no choice but to just keep doing what I'm told.

\textbf{Counselor:} That's a very difficult situation. An environment where it's hard to express your opinions can be a significant mental burden. However, your health and well-being are also very important. If possible, do you have any opportunities to consult with trusted colleagues or another supervisor at work? Also, it's important to have time to take care of yourself, such as stress relief methods in your private life.

\textbf{Client:} I've consulted a bit with my colleagues, but everyone seems to have similar concerns... In my private life, I go to the gym to exercise and relieve stress, but I still feel like there's something unsettled deep inside.

