\subsection{Evaluation Metrics}

%\textcolor{red}{Evaluating multi-label classification performance requires a nuanced approach due to overlapping class memberships and class imbalance.} 
In line with established practices in remote sensing~\cite{you2023multi}, we report both macro-averaged and micro-averaged precision and F1-scores. \textbf{Macro-averaging} treats each class equally by computing metrics independently per class and then averaging them. This is crucial for overall system performance, ensuring that rare land cover types—prevalent in long-tail distributions—are not neglected. In contrast, \textbf{micro-averaging} aggregates all true positives, false positives, and false negatives across classes before computing the metrics. This provides a global view of the model’s predictive performance, especially appropriate in scenarios with high class imbalance. 
%\textcolor{red}{By reporting both macro and micro scores, we ensure a comprehensive evaluation that captures both per-class and overall model behavior.} 
These metrics align with evaluation protocols used in the BigEarthNet V2.0 benchmark~\cite{bigearthnet2}.
