\section{Application on regression tasks}
\label{app_B}

The experimental results on ChemBench demonstrate that our RLDBF method enhances LLMs' ability to uncover structural and numerical relationships in molecular prediction takss, suggesting that RLDBF may implicitly refine molecular representations in the latent embedding space, thereby unlocking the potential of large models for regression tasks. 
To validate this hypothesis, we conducted experiments on regression task: 
Coulombic efficiency prediction~\citep{kim2023data} for electrolytes. 
We employ a unified network architecture: the hidden output of the last LlamaDecoderLayer is first extracted as the molecular embedding, which is then processed through a simple MLP comprising two fully connected layers to generate the final prediction.

\paragraph{CE Prediction}

